node_modules/

# Logs are ignored by default, with three deliberate exceptions below.
#
# The run logs under interop/results/, interop/negative-controls/ and
# benchmarks/ are PUBLISHED EVIDENCE, not incidental output: the interop
# claim is graded from them, so they are committed on purpose. 460 of them
# are tracked today (`git ls-files '*.log' | wc -l`).
#
# They were originally force-added past the bare `*.log` rule. That was
# fragile: once a path is tracked, .gitignore no longer applies to it, so
# `git add -A` stages further edits to those files with no warning, while
# the rule still reads as if all logs were ignored. The negations below make
# the intent explicit, so nobody adds a log to one of these directories
# assuming it will be ignored, and nobody deletes the rule assuming the
# tracked logs are accidents.
#
# Before committing new logs, check them for machine detail: grep tracked
# files for Windows and POSIX home-directory prefixes, and for non-loopback
# IPv4. Measured 2026-09-19, the tracked logs carry neither. The only
# address appearing in any of the 460 is 127.0.0.1, and no tracked file
# matches a home-directory prefix. That follows from the harnesses binding
# to loopback and the runner recording directory basenames rather than
# paths; it is not a guarantee about future logs.
*.log
!interop/results/**/*.log
!interop/negative-controls/**/*.log
!benchmarks/**/*.log
